  "description": "A layered ecological contemporary planting built around Georgia and Dos' palette of silvers, purples, soft greens and smoky blues. Olive, Jacaranda and October Glory Maple form the upper canopy, while Westringia, Rosemary, Euphorbia, Echium and Smokebush anchor the mid structure with year-round form. Through the middle layers, Miscanthus, Gaura, Salvia and Limonium bring movement and extended seasonal colour. Native Violet, Dichondra and Pratia stitch together a living ground layer that protects soil and holds moisture. Designed by Gardener & Son to feel relaxed, immersive and full of seasonal life — a planting that becomes more resilient and ecologically connected as it matures.",
